{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":252670,"ns":0,"title":"Absolute continuity","extract":"In calculus and real analysis, absolute continuity is a regularity property of functions that is stronger than uniform continuity, and hence continuity. The notion of absolute continuity allows one to generalize the fundamental theorem of calculus, originally in the framework of Riemann integration, to Lebesgue integration.","description":"Form of continuity for functions","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}